// the app's own dice font is embedded, so the exporters no longer drop the tokens: this turns prose into RUNS, text and
// symbols in order, and `pdfSymbolKit` (beside ensurePDFLib) measures, wraps, fits and draws them. Both exporters and the
// signature block go through it; there is no second path.
//   · It MATCHES only the tokens the shared table knows (window.SWRPGDice.BRACKET_TOKENS), built from that table's keys,
//     so it is a matcher and never a deleter. A bracket-shaped token the table does not know is removed from the text run
//     by `plainTextGlyphless` above, the one stripper (H1-H4) — the same nothing that `glyphText` draws on screen (C-Q1-2).
//   · Each symbol prints from ONE font, public/fonts/sw-rpg-icons.woff (MIT; it carries every die shape and every result).
//     The six dice whose screen glyph is the Genesys font's letter take the same shape from this font (PDF_DIE_SHAPE), and
//     the screen's FILL FAMILY (light / Force die hollow, Force pip half) takes this font's hollow and half marks.
//   · A token the table knows that this font cannot draw THROWS — the export fails loudly; it never prints a silent gap.
